\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Planar radial vectors from the origin $O=(0,0)$, head-to-tail polygon closure, and the Diophantine Pell minimum at order four. (a)~Radial vectors $z_{ij}\mathbf  r_{ij}$ on square \#70 across the three concentric rings $R_{\mathrm  {in}},R_{\mathrm  {mid}},R_{\mathrm  {out}}$, with ring dipoles $\mathbf  d_{\mathrm  {in}}=(3,0)$, $\mathbf  d_{\mathrm  {out}}=(15,0)$, and $\mathbf  d_{\mathrm  {mid}}=(-18,0)$. (b)~Ordered head-to-tail placement closes the $16$-gon at linear lengths $\alpha =1$ (\#70) and inverse lengths $\alpha ^*=-1$ (\#45), whereas unit lengths $\alpha =0$ (\#635) leave a nonzero gap $\mathbf  B_{\mathrm  {unit}}(S)$ (magenta). (c)~Census of $\|\mathbf  v(S)\|_2$ versus $\|\mathbf  u(S)\|_2$ across all $880$ squares against the irrational balance line $\|\mathbf  v\|=\sqrt  {5}\,\|\mathbf  u\|$, with the eight Pell-minimum squares ($v/u=9/4$) marked by red stars. (d)~Resultant norm $\|\mathbf  B_{z,r^\alpha }(S)\|_2$ versus exponent $\alpha $, showing the universal zero at $\alpha =1$ and second roots at $\alpha ^*=-1$ (\#45), $-0.050$ (\#70), and $+3$ (\#286).}}{6}{figure.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ring-vectors}{{2}{6}{Planar radial vectors from the origin $O=(0,0)$, head-to-tail polygon closure, and the Diophantine Pell minimum at order four. (a)~Radial vectors $z_{ij}\mathbf r_{ij}$ on square \#70 across the three concentric rings $R_{\mathrm {in}},R_{\mathrm {mid}},R_{\mathrm {out}}$, with ring dipoles $\mathbf d_{\mathrm {in}}=(3,0)$, $\mathbf d_{\mathrm {out}}=(15,0)$, and $\mathbf d_{\mathrm {mid}}=(-18,0)$. (b)~Ordered head-to-tail placement closes the $16$-gon at linear lengths $\alpha =1$ (\#70) and inverse lengths $\alpha ^*=-1$ (\#45), whereas unit lengths $\alpha =0$ (\#635) leave a nonzero gap $\mathbf B_{\mathrm {unit}}(S)$ (magenta). (c)~Census of $\|\mathbf v(S)\|_2$ versus $\|\mathbf u(S)\|_2$ across all $880$ squares against the irrational balance line $\|\mathbf v\|=\sqrt {5}\,\|\mathbf u\|$, with the eight Pell-minimum squares ($v/u=9/4$) marked by red stars. (d)~Resultant norm $\|\mathbf B_{z,r^\alpha }(S)\|_2$ versus exponent $\alpha $, showing the universal zero at $\alpha =1$ and second roots at $\alpha ^*=-1$ (\#45), $-0.050$ (\#70), and $+3$ (\#286)}{figure.16}{}}
