\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Three-dimensional radial spoke sculptures from the origin $O=(0,0,0)$ under variable length and tip weight. (a)~Natural $16$-spoke sculpture $\mathbf  p_{ij}$ ($\beta =1$, orange $z_{ij}>0$, blue $z_{ij}<0$) of non-associative square \#70, balancing identically at $O$. (b)~Trimming all spokes to the unit sphere $S^2$ ($\beta =0$, equal weights) leaves a non-zero resultant $\mathbf  V_0=(0,0.773,0)$ (magenta arrow) on \#70, whereas antipodal pairs cancel on D\"urer \#175. (c)~Minimum-variance positive tip weights $w_{ij}^*\in [0.72,1.19]$ (gold-rimmed for $w_{ij}^*>1$) restore exact unit-sphere balance $\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ w_{ij}^*\hat  {\mathbf  p}_{ij}=\mathbf  0$. (d)~Normalized resultant $\|\mathbf  V_\beta (S;1)\|_2/\bar  R^{\beta -1}$ versus exponent $\beta $, showing universal balance at $\beta =1$, second roots $\beta ^*\ne  1$ on Group~VI squares (\#70, \#45, \#376), and universal vertical vanishing $(\mathbf  V_3)_z=0$ at $\beta =3$ (gold dashed curve).}}{8}{figure.26}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:origin-vectors-3d}{{3}{8}{Three-dimensional radial spoke sculptures from the origin $O=(0,0,0)$ under variable length and tip weight. (a)~Natural $16$-spoke sculpture $\mathbf p_{ij}$ ($\beta =1$, orange $z_{ij}>0$, blue $z_{ij}<0$) of non-associative square \#70, balancing identically at $O$. (b)~Trimming all spokes to the unit sphere $S^2$ ($\beta =0$, equal weights) leaves a non-zero resultant $\mathbf V_0=(0,0.773,0)$ (magenta arrow) on \#70, whereas antipodal pairs cancel on D\"urer \#175. (c)~Minimum-variance positive tip weights $w_{ij}^*\in [0.72,1.19]$ (gold-rimmed for $w_{ij}^*>1$) restore exact unit-sphere balance $\sum w_{ij}^*\hat {\mathbf p}_{ij}=\mathbf 0$. (d)~Normalized resultant $\|\mathbf V_\beta (S;1)\|_2/\bar R^{\beta -1}$ versus exponent $\beta $, showing universal balance at $\beta =1$, second roots $\beta ^*\ne 1$ on Group~VI squares (\#70, \#45, \#376), and universal vertical vanishing $(\mathbf V_3)_z=0$ at $\beta =3$ (gold dashed curve)}{figure.26}{}}
