\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The three non-associative order-four magic squares whose uniform solid $\mathcal  G_0(S)$ has exact centre of mass $\mathbf  c_0(S)=\mathbf  0$, together with their inner core $\mathcal  G_1(S)=\operatorname  {conv}(P_S\setminus \operatorname  {vert}\mathcal  G_0(S))$. All three squares lie in Dudeney's Group~VI and have $12$ outer vertices and $4$ inner points (spanning a planar parallelogram in \#86 and a 3D tetrahedron in \#739 and \#756) whose centroid $\mathbf  c_1(S)$ is also $\mathbf  0$.}}{13}{table.51}\protected@file@percent }
