\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Nested `diamond-in-a-diamond' convex layers $\mathcal  G_0(S)\supset \mathcal  G_1(S)$ and centre-of-mass restoration. (a)~Denser-core Gem \#673 ($(V_0,V_1)=(8,8)$) and (b)~hollow-cavity Gem \#54 ($(V_0,V_1)=(10,6)$, $1$-swap sibling of \#45), showing the translucent outer hull $\mathcal  G_0(S)$ around the inner core $\mathcal  G_1(S)$ with 2D fulcrum lever diagrams below. On \#673, $\mathbf  c_0$ (green circle) and $\mathbf  c_1$ (gold diamond) lie on opposite sides of $O$, balancing via a heavier inner core ($\Delta \rho _1/\rho _0=+5/4$). On \#54, volumetric simplex weighting pulls $\mathbf  c_0=(0,19/324,0)$ onto the $+y$ side alongside $\mathbf  c_1=(0,29/68,0)$, so a $98.3\%$ hollow core cavity ($\Delta \rho _1/\rho _0=-57/58$) restores balance at $O$. (c)~Census of nested layer dimensions and solid balance mechanisms across all $880$ order-four magic squares.}}{14}{figure.56}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:nested-diamonds}{{5}{14}{Nested `diamond-in-a-diamond' convex layers $\mathcal G_0(S)\supset \mathcal G_1(S)$ and centre-of-mass restoration. (a)~Denser-core Gem \#673 ($(V_0,V_1)=(8,8)$) and (b)~hollow-cavity Gem \#54 ($(V_0,V_1)=(10,6)$, $1$-swap sibling of \#45), showing the translucent outer hull $\mathcal G_0(S)$ around the inner core $\mathcal G_1(S)$ with 2D fulcrum lever diagrams below. On \#673, $\mathbf c_0$ (green circle) and $\mathbf c_1$ (gold diamond) lie on opposite sides of $O$, balancing via a heavier inner core ($\Delta \rho _1/\rho _0=+5/4$). On \#54, volumetric simplex weighting pulls $\mathbf c_0=(0,19/324,0)$ onto the $+y$ side alongside $\mathbf c_1=(0,29/68,0)$, so a $98.3\%$ hollow core cavity ($\Delta \rho _1/\rho _0=-57/58$) restores balance at $O$. (c)~Census of nested layer dimensions and solid balance mechanisms across all $880$ order-four magic squares}{figure.56}{}}
